# Base URL of the Cloud Server the dashboard talks to. Copy this file to ".env"
# (gitignored) and fill it in for your deployment.
#
# Discovery is served by the Cloud Server at <base>/discovery, so this single
# address covers both planes — there is no separate discovery URL to configure.
# Point it at whatever port the Cloud Server listens on (8002 by default; some
# deployments run PORT=8000).
#
# Dev:  leave blank to use the Vite proxy (/v1 -> http://localhost:8002), which
#       sidesteps CORS entirely. When set, it drives BOTH the client's base URL
#       and the dev proxy target.
# Prod: set to the deployed cloud URL, e.g. https://api.yourdomain.com — it is
#       baked into the build, and the server's CORS_ORIGINS must include this
#       dashboard's origin.
#
# Either way a user can override this at runtime from the app's "Server:" field
# on the login page (stored in localStorage as cloud_base_url); that takes
# precedence over this value and needs no rebuild.
VITE_CLOUD_URL=
